\title{Regression Accelerated Bayesian Additive Regression Trees Learner}
\description{
Accelerated Bayesian additive regression trees (XBART) for regression.
Calls \code{XBART::XBART()} from package 'XBART'.

The prediction is the mean over the sweeps after the burn-in period, as recommended by the upstream package.
XBART draws random numbers from its own generator and ignores \code{set.seed()}.
Set the \code{random_seed} parameter to obtain reproducible results.
Messages printed by XBART during training are suppressed unless \code{verbose} is \code{TRUE}.
}
\section{Installation}{

Package 'XBART' is not on CRAN and has to be installed from GitHub via
\code{remotes::install_github("JingyuHe/XBART")}.
It links against the GNU Scientific Library (GSL),
which has to be installed on the system first, e.g. via \verb{apt install libgsl-dev} or \verb{brew install gsl}.
}

\section{Initial parameter values}{

\itemize{
\item \code{num_trees} is initialized to 100 and \code{num_sweeps} to 40, because \code{XBART::XBART()} has no defaults for them.
\item \code{nthread} is initialized to 1 to avoid conflicts with parallelization via \CRANpkg{future}.
}
}

